WEBVTT

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.880
Of course, some people will not be old enough.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.880
In these kinds of situations, we will want our programs to do something else when the

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.080
condition is false.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:20.100
In order to do this, we will want to expand our if statements to include an else statement.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:25.180
The commands contained in this else statement only run if the Boolean condition in the if

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.820
statement is false.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:32.920
In App Lab, you can add an else statement by either dragging out the if else block or

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:36.480
by clicking the plus symbol in the bottom right corner of the if block.
